# Prototype (`client/`) — Active Demo Artifact

`client/` is the interactive prototype presented to the client. It is being enhanced to feel production-grade (plan: `docs/PROTOTYPE_ENHANCEMENT_PLAN.md`). It is **not** the production codebase — that is `server/`, `frontend/`, `app/`.

## Boundaries
- Self-contained: no backend calls, no auth servers; data lives in stores persisted to `localStorage`. Do not import from or into the production apps.
- No new runtime dependencies without a stated reason (routing is hash-based; hashing uses Web Crypto).
- Behaviour previews the production spec: permissions and scopes from `docs/platform/06` §h, states/enums from `docs/platform/02`, reference formats from `docs/platform/00` §5.2.

## Code conventions
- Colours, spacing, radii, shadows only via tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css`; **no hex literals or ad-hoc inline colours in `.tsx`**. Use the primitives in `src/components/ui/` before writing custom markup.
- Identity via `currentUser`/`useCan('module:action')`/`useScope()` from `src/auth/` — never `role === 'x'` or name-string matching in views.
- Stores are the single source of truth; views never keep private copies of seed data. Dates relative to `today()` from `src/lib/clock.ts`; reference numbers via `nextRef(prefix)`.
- Every view handles loading (skeleton), empty, and error states, in both themes.
- Bilingual: every user-facing string through `t(en, bn, lang)`; keep EN and BN both filled.
- Demo-only controls (persona switch, reset, scenarios) live only in the hidden demo panel, never in product UI.

## Verify
`cd client && npm run build` must pass; check the changed screens in light and dark; check with at least two personas (an approver and an employee/driver).
